Ukraine's Defense Forces have struck more than 45 Russian oil, chemical, and defense industry facilities in October and November 2026, some of them multiple times:
▪️ Novoshakhtinsk oil refinery, Rostov region (November 23);
▪️ LUKOIL-Permnefteorgsintez oil refinery, Perm region (October 7; reportedly struck again on November 23, awaiting official confirmation);
▪️ Kaleykino oil pumping station, Tatarstan (November 19; reportedly struck again on November 23, awaiting official confirmation);
▪️ Dorogobuzh chemical plant, Smolensk region (November 10 and 20);
▪️ Ilsky oil refinery, Krasnodar region (November 15-16 and 18);
▪️ Afipsky oil refinery, Krasnodar region (November 6 and 18);
▪️ Gazprom Neftekhim Salavat petrochemical complex, Bashkortostan (October 8 and November 17);
▪️ Bashneft-Ufaneftekhim oil refinery, Bashkortostan (November 17);
▪️ Flash Energy oil depot, Azov, Rostov region (November 16);
▪️ Transit-Express fuel transshipment terminal, Azov, Rostov region (November 16);
▪️ Azovskaya oil depot, Azov, Rostov region (November 16);
▪️ Monolit aviation manufacturing plant, Bryansk region (November 15);
▪️ Nizhnekamskneftekhim petrochemical complex, Tatarstan (November 15);
▪️ TAIF-NK oil refinery, Tatarstan (November 15);
▪️ Samara oil pumping station, Samara region (October 2 and 10; November 2, 7 and 13);
▪️ Ionos drone production facility, Rostov-on-Don, Rostov region (November 13);
